<http://data.silknow.org/object/efdee35b-76b5-39ce-ab67-9f3f6964fec1>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "embroidered, 1800s, Turkish"@en , "? embroidered with silk in double darning on the diagonal, double running in a line and needleweaving for the border. There are two motifs which alternate along the border: (1) a circular motif with a green blossom at its centre surrounded by eight curved leaves, white with a black spot alternating with brown; these are surrounded by small inward-facing U-shaped motifs in light blue or white and finally at each 'corner' is a brown and light blue curved serrated leaf. (2) Two curved, joined green stems each bearing brown or white flowerheads [these are outlined in black with a black centre]; there are small leaves in green, white and light blue.  The direction of this motif alternates: outward facing and inward facing."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/e1a2b5ad-3e94-342a-b35a-5cc310ce5491> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "embroidered, 1800s, Turkish"@en , "? embroidered with silk in double darning on the diagonal, double running in a line and needleweaving for the border. There are two motifs which alternate along the border: (1) a circular motif with a green blossom at its centre surrounded by eight curved leaves, white with a black spot alternating with brown; these are surrounded by small inward-facing U-shaped motifs in light blue or white and finally at each 'corner' is a brown and light blue curved serrated leaf. (2) Two curved, joined green stems each bearing brown or white flowerheads [these are outlined in black with a black centre]; there are small leaves in green, white and light blue.  The direction of this motif alternates: outward facing and inward facing."@en ;
